WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.936
-President Trump has spent
the last week creating crises

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:05.838
and then pretending
he solved those crises.

00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:08.207
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:09.776
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:12.145 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:15.181
-Well, it's been another
roller coaster few days

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.216
with our split personality
president creating

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:18.918
a bunch of problems
and then turning around

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.653
and claiming he solved
those problems.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.156
Every day with this guy
is like "Fight Club."

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.591
One of these days we're going
to find him in the parking lot

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:27.794
outside the White House
beating the crap out of himself.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.095
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.596
One day he's threatening
war with Iran.

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:32.799
The next day he's claiming
he stopped a war with Iran.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.400
One day he's threatening
to deport millions

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.902
and rip apart migrant families,

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:38.237
the next day he's saying
he delayed the deportations.

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:40.072
It's almost like he saw
the polls,

00:00:40.072 --> 00:00:42.342
and instead of running
against the Democrats in 2020,

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.843
he decided to run against
himself.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:44.610
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.845
[ As Trump ] "Vote for me.

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.947
I'm the only one who
can stop Donald Trump!"

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.315
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:50.683
[ Normal voice ]
Trump swings wildly

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.452
from one position to the next

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:55.254
because he has no moral compass
or a strategic vision.

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:57.991
And that combination
of ignorance and impulsiveness

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.893
has been on full display during
his administration's march

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:02.295
toward war with Iran.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.996
Now war with Iran
would be catastrophic.

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:05.831
It would be reckless,
unjustified, and illegal.

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:07.933
And yet, many of the people
around Trump

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:10.703
have been agitating for a war
with Iran for years.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.239
Trump, meanwhile, has repeatedly
refused to divulge

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:16.108
any details about what
his administration might do.

00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:19.678
-Mr. President,
will you go to war with Iran?

00:01:19.678 --> 00:01:20.946
-I hope not.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.946 --> 00:01:23.416
-If they reach
the uranium limits on the 27th,

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.984
will you take additional action?

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:26.652
-I won't say what I'll do.

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:28.254
-Mr. President,
how will you respond?

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:29.788
-You'll find out.

00:01:29.788 --> 00:01:31.658
-Are you willing to go to war
with Iran?

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:33.626
-You'll find out.
You'll find out.

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.761
-What, we'll find out?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.761 --> 00:01:37.597
You're talking about
a massive war that would

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.432
destabilize the Middle East.

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.768
You can't talk about it like
you're hosting "Dateline."

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.169
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:46.172
"They weren't sure if they
were heading to war with Iran,

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:49.342
oh, but they'd soon find out."

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:50.909
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:53.279
Trump doesn't answer questions
about his plans

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.547
because he has no plans.

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.449
He waivers from one position
to the next

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.983
based on the last person
he talked to

00:01:57.983 --> 00:01:59.385
or something he saw on TV.

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.488
If he watches Sean Hannity's
show, he wants to go to war.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.923
If he watches Tucker Carlson's
show, he wants to pull back.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:06.392
And if he watches QVC, he ends
up buying a bunch of jewelry.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.027
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.963
And that reckless impulsivity
was on full display last week

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:14.734
when it was reported that Trump
had okayed an attack on Iran

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:17.269
and then changed his mind
at the last minute.

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:20.506
-"The New York Times" reporting
the president authorized

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:24.176
military strikes against Iran,
then called them off.

00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:28.147
"The Times" says the president
initially approved attacks

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:29.782
on a handful of Iranian targets

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:31.117
like radar
and missile batteries.

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.119
"The Times" reports there were
ships in position.

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:34.353
There were planes in the air

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:36.488
when the president
walked the whole thing back.

00:02:36.488 --> 00:02:39.158
-On Monday, they shot down
an unmanned drone

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:41.193
flying in international waters.

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:43.563
"We were cocked and loaded
to retaliate last night

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:47.100
on three different sites when
I asked, how many will die?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.870
150 people, sir,
was the answer from a general.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.639
Ten minutes before the strike,
I stopped it."

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.675
-This tweet is Trump
in a nutshell.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.244
He makes it genuinely difficult
for you to focus on the fact

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.545
that he almost started
a disastrous

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:01.780
and unconstitutional war with
Iran because he used

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:05.251
the wrong "sights" and used
the phrase, "cocked and loaded."

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.286
[ Laughter ]
It's "locked and loaded."

00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:10.356
"Cocked and loaded" sounds like
the name of a Tom Green movie

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.092
where a guy takes a road trip
with a rooster.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:15.762
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:18.097
Now, it's obviously a good thing

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.565
that we did not go to war
with Iran.

00:03:19.565 --> 00:03:21.767
But it's terrifying that it
even got this far.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.603
Trump wants us all to praise him
for pulling back

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.872
from a catastrophic situation
that he almost started.

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:28.608
Praise he doesn't deserve

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:30.743
as Senator Bernie Sanders
argued on Sunday.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.311
-Was President Trump's decision
this week

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:34.414
to call off that strike
the right one?

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:37.183
-[ Chuckles ] See,
it's like somebody

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:42.521
setting a fire
to a basket full of paper

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:44.023
and then putting it out.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:46.693
He helped create the crisis.
And then he stopped the attacks.

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:49.094
The idea that we're looking at
a president of the United States

00:03:49.094 --> 00:03:53.298
who, number one,
thinks that a war with Iran

00:03:53.298 --> 00:03:55.902
is something that might be good
for this country...

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:57.536
-He was just doing
a limited strike.

00:03:57.536 --> 00:04:00.406
-Oh, just a limited strike.
Oh. Well, I'm sor-ry.

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:02.107
[ Laughter ]
I just didn't know that

00:04:02.107 --> 00:04:04.477
it's okay to simply attack
another country with bombs

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:06.746
just for limited --
That's an act of warfare.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:10.349
-He's right. And also, you got
to love his old-man sarcasm.

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:11.750
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.686
[ As Sanders ] "What are you
always doing on your phone?"

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:16.021
[ Normal voice ] "I'm just
sending an emoji, grandpa."

00:04:16.021 --> 00:04:17.690
[ As Sanders ]
"Oh, just an emoji!

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.925
[ Laughter ]
You see, when I was growing up,

00:04:19.925 --> 00:04:22.061
the only emojis we had
were our faces.

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.963
So when our friends
wanted to know how I was,

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:25.631
they wouldn't look down there.
They would look up here.

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:27.567
And that's how they knew
I was grumpy!"

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.502
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:31.003
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:34.106
[ Normal voice ] And on top
of everything else,

00:04:34.106 --> 00:04:35.608
Trump's account of how

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:37.676
this episode unfolded
makes no sense.

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:38.978
Ex-national security officials

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:41.280
who have actually been in these
kinds of briefings

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.682
said it was unlikely
the president would find out

00:04:43.682 --> 00:04:46.185
at the last minute what
the casualty count would be.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:49.956
-Is it plausible in any way
the president is first informed

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:52.524
of casualty estimates that close

00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:56.462
to the actual commission
of the strike?

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:59.665
-No. The whole thing here
is very -- is very strange.

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:02.668
-Does that make sense?
-No. It's not credible in terms

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:06.005
of whether he was briefed
or not at that late time.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:07.773
It's laid out right
in the beginning.

00:05:07.773 --> 00:05:09.275
It's like the first
PowerPoint slide.

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:12.244
-Okay.
Well, see, there's your problem.

00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:15.448
You can't give him information
on a PowerPoint slide.

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:16.882
When Donald Trump hears
PowerPoint,

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:18.951
he slides out of the room.

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:20.987
"We'd like to start
our PowerPoint presentation."

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:22.087
[ As Trump ] "PowerPoint,
good, good, good.

00:05:22.087 --> 00:05:24.123
Yeah, get that started.
Okay.

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:25.224
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.894
Okay. Okay.

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:29.562
Oh, okay.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:33.699
[ Applause ]
Oh."

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:36.034
[ Normal voice ] If you really,
really want Donald Trump

00:05:36.034 --> 00:05:37.336
to pay attention to a briefing,

00:05:37.336 --> 00:05:39.505
you got to write it somewhere
he's going to look

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:40.873
like a mirror.

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:42.708
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.708 --> 00:05:44.844
And listening to the president's
incoherent explanation

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:47.013
of how he made the decision
is even more terrifying.

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.847
Here's Trump narrating
his thought process

00:05:48.847 --> 00:05:51.483
and explaining how he was
ready to order a military strike

00:05:51.483 --> 00:05:54.587
on Iran until it occurred
to him, at the last minute,

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:57.156
to ask what might seem like
an important question.

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:59.759
-We had something ready to go,
subject to my approval.

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:03.395
And they came in. And they came
in about a half an hour before.

00:06:03.395 --> 00:06:05.431
They said, "Sir,
we're about ready to go."

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:07.166
I said,
"I want a better definition."

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:08.800
-Planes in the air?
Were planes in the air?

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.302
-No, no,
we're about ready to go.

00:06:10.302 --> 00:06:13.238
No, but they would have been
pretty soon.

00:06:13.238 --> 00:06:15.407
And things would have happened
to a point

00:06:15.407 --> 00:06:17.610
where you wouldn't turn back
or couldn't turn back.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:20.213
So they came and they said,

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:21.914
"Sir, we're ready to go.
We'd like a decision."

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:24.016
I said, "I want to know
something before you go.

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:26.352
How many people will be killed?"

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:28.587
In this case, Iranians.

00:06:28.587 --> 00:06:31.824
I said, "How many people
are going to be killed?"

00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:33.959
"Sir, I'd like to get
back to you on that."

00:06:33.959 --> 00:06:35.694
Great people, these generals.

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:41.000
They said -- Came back, said,
"Sir, approximately 150."

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.035
And I thought about it
for a second.

00:06:43.035 --> 00:06:47.607
I said, you know what, they shot
down an unmanned drone,

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:49.742
plane, whatever
you want to call it.

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:52.344
-No.
Whatever I want to call it?

00:06:52.344 --> 00:06:54.013
I want to call it a goose!

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:55.948
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.948 --> 00:07:00.586
"Shoot down the goose, papa!"

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:04.323
Why don't we all call it a drone
since that's what it is?

00:07:04.323 --> 00:07:07.326
If it was a drone, then by
definition, it was unmanned.

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:09.028
There's no such thing
as a manned drone.

00:07:09.028 --> 00:07:10.530
You never see a drone
flying around

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.866
with a dude hanging off of it.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:13.866 --> 00:07:15.668
Not only is this story
of what happened

00:07:15.668 --> 00:07:17.035
in this particular case
incoherent,

00:07:17.035 --> 00:07:19.738
but so is Trump's overall policy
toward Iran.

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:21.274
Just listen to him today
in the oval office

00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:22.808
announcing new sanctions on Iran

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:24.744
and talking about President
Obama's nuclear agreement

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:26.545
with Iran,
an agreement Trump tore up

00:07:26.545 --> 00:07:28.381
despite the fact
that his own administration

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:30.216
said Iran was complying with it.

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:33.652
-They've done many other things
aside from the individual drone.

00:07:33.652 --> 00:07:34.920
You saw the tankers.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.588
And we know of other things
that were done also

00:07:36.588 --> 00:07:37.823
which were not good.

00:07:37.823 --> 00:07:40.792
The agreement that was signed
was a disaster.

00:07:40.792 --> 00:07:44.630
It was not doing
what it was supposed to do.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:46.531
Many bad things
were taking place.

00:07:46.531 --> 00:07:50.169
So I look forward to discussing

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:53.906
whatever I have to discuss with
anybody that wants to speak.

00:07:53.906 --> 00:07:56.108
-Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:58.344
Slow down with
all the specifics!

00:07:58.344 --> 00:07:59.645
[ Laughter ]

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:01.046
It's amazing to think
there used to be a time

00:08:01.046 --> 00:08:02.781
when reporters covering
the White House

00:08:02.781 --> 00:08:04.783
had to furiously scribble notes
in their pads

00:08:04.783 --> 00:08:06.452
to keep track of all
the complicated details

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:07.853
of treaties or legislation.

00:08:07.853 --> 00:08:09.454
And now when they cover
the president,

00:08:09.454 --> 00:08:11.023
they just have to write stuff
down like,

00:08:11.023 --> 00:08:13.659
"Things that were not good,
bad things taking place,

00:08:13.659 --> 00:08:16.228
cocked and loaded."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:16.228 --> 00:08:18.497
But the important question here
is what is the end game?

00:08:18.497 --> 00:08:19.665
What does Trump want?

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:21.833
Does he want war?
Does he want a new deal?

00:08:21.833 --> 00:08:24.803
If so, how would that new deal
differ from the old deal?

00:08:24.803 --> 00:08:26.806
And why would Iran ever agree
to a new deal

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:28.240
after the last deal
they negotiated

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:29.475
was torn up for no reason?

00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:30.809
These are all important
questions,

00:08:30.809 --> 00:08:33.212
and yet the president
clearly has no answers.

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:36.949
-Mr. President, is your goal to
negotiate a new deal with Iran?

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:39.784
Mr. President, is your goal
to negotiate a new deal --

00:08:39.784 --> 00:08:40.786
-We would love to be able

00:08:40.786 --> 00:08:42.488
to negotiate a deal
if they want to.

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:43.889
If they don't want to,
that's fine, too.

00:08:43.889 --> 00:08:45.157
-Oh, my God, man.

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:47.593
Next time just throw
a smoke pellet and run away.

00:08:47.593 --> 00:08:50.529
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.529 --> 00:08:52.197
In the past few days,
we've seen the president

00:08:52.197 --> 00:08:53.599
take us to the brink of war
with Iran,

00:08:53.599 --> 00:08:55.734
threaten to inflict more cruelty
on migrant families,

00:08:55.734 --> 00:08:58.371
all while being accused of
a horrific sexual assault.

00:08:58.371 --> 00:09:00.506
The question now is
what more will it take

00:09:00.506 --> 00:09:01.574
to impeach this guy?

00:09:01.574 --> 00:09:02.942
I don't know if he'll win
a second term.

00:09:02.942 --> 00:09:04.677
But at this point,
all I can say is...

00:09:04.677 --> 00:09:07.746
-I hope not.
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:07.746 --> 00:09:09.481
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:09.481 --> 00:09:11.350 line:0%
♪♪

